      "settlementKey": "marrowynd:Myrkwake",
      "description": "Fritsch Gamebell is a warm, nervous Gnome mechanic who survived the Nefaric Veil by making himself too useful to collar, exile, or kill. He keeps the arena games, prize engines, ticket dispensers, training machines, and warded obstacle rooms running with a healer’s patience and a handyman’s instinct, always patching broken people and broken gears with the same tired kindness. At the Myrkwake Archive, Fritsch manages the arena floor as something between arcade-master, field medic, and reluctant moral compass, making sure the games stay dangerous enough to satisfy raiders but not so lethal that every guest becomes a body. He dislikes ichor-addled cruelty, quietly rigs safety releases into the machines, and has a gentle way of helping frightened fighters feel like they still have a choice, even when the whole Carnival insists they do not.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Myrkwake is a Town in Marrowynd, under Representative Democracy, with high danger, Ocean Surface floating settlement, Underwater without reefs terrain. Local records favor Neutral, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Elf — Sea Elf, Tortle, Genasi — Water Genasi. Gnome reads through the Deep Gnome entry of the race compendium, within Dwarven and Gnomish Kin, marked by Marduthor. Deep gnomes, or svirfneblin, are adapted to life in the deep subterranean world. They are cautious, stealthy, and highly resourceful in dangerous underground environments. Table cues: Gnome, Darkvision, Gift of the Svirfneblin, Gnomish Magic Resistance; starting tendency Neutral - Lawful - Neutral - Honorable.",
